7592186436064 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436070 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436070 1077 "selection" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436070 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436061 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436070 1079 #uuid "c212f72a-279f-54ef-b120-28592cf65c59" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436067 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1069 "q-97031" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1071 "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{4},$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1072 #uuid "132fd44c-38e5-5ebe-8c05-231eab1b1859" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436071 1074 "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436070 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1069 "q-8028" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1071 "Find the standard matrix that  represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1072 #uuid "43480c80-f56c-525c-8e3a-4535ddf6aa7b" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436072 1074 "We require a $2\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x+(-1)y+1z \\\\ 1x+(-1)y+(-1)z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z \\\\ x-y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436069 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1069 "q-96976" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1071 "$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\,T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+ax \\\\ bx+4y \\\\ cy+3x\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1072 #uuid "93b16baf-60a0-5351-9b6d-e1dbecba8523" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436073 1074 "Given the vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5x+3y \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ 3x-y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ -2x+4y \\\\ -y+3x\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y+5x \\\\ (-2)x+4y \\\\ (-1)y+3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a+b+c=5+(-2)+(-1)=2.$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436068 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1069 "q-140366" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1071 "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{4},$ where\n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1072 #uuid "d43f6aa4-a331-53b3-b9d7-aed1378d0872" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true] [17592186436074 1074 "We require a $4\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n    \n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}(-4)x+5y+(-1)z \\\\ 3x+(-2)y+7z \\\\ (-6)x+1y+0z \\\\ (-3)x+8y+0z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4x-z+5y \\\\ 3x+7z-2y \\\\ -6x+y \\\\ 8y-3x\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534789 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0dde21cb-d15c-5e2a-8f75-04c7a50e62ec" 17592186436047 "answer-2966ef61-eca9-5559-a74b-278b39bfedaf" 17592186436048 "answer-3c79ee30-af5f-5bcf-8919-2afd0111f993" 17592186436049 "answer-3e3fc592-6115-55a4-af5d-3458bd239697" 17592186436050 "answer-3fb5a88e-2c16-50c0-a11b-1857fef41b83" 17592186436051 "answer-4be85799-67c5-5191-9977-b583cddea1c0" 17592186436052 "answer-4df16430-0c5c-51d3-b20c-0818ccaee58e" 17592186436053 "answer-628defca-3da6-558b-ae06-2b8a5c25cb83" 17592186436054 "answer-684703ee-abb2-545a-9b7e-ac869bc848c7" 17592186436055 "answer-848ef172-7da8-5389-b025-51826e69cb7f" 17592186436056 "answer-89fb8e93-7da5-59dc-a467-6a051fba4e92" 17592186436057 "answer-8db1b7fe-f0f1-5029-831c-002